# Claude Code's local permission/session config can end up echoing literal command text
# (including secrets typed into a terminal command, like the USDA_API_KEY curl test this
# project ran) — keep it out of version control same as local.properties.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Transient per-session lock file (pid/session id), not project state.
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Round-by-round dev journal -- carries a lot of specific personal context (the user's own
# patterns, why certain product calls were made) that has no reason to be in a public repo's
# history. Local-only, same "lives here, not synced" treatment as local.properties. Scrubbed
# from all prior git history via git-filter-repo when the repo went public -- never re-add this
# to tracking.
HANDOFF.md
